# Docker dev sync after source change

When finishing work that changes **frontend/** or **backend/** sources **and** the user relies on the **local Docker** stack (`docker-compose` / Compose V2 with this repo’s `docker/docker-compose.yml`), the **implementing agent** should run **`./scripts/docker-dev-sync.sh`** from the repository root **after** unit tests (or document why it failed / was skipped), so `dist/logmng-offline-<VERSION>/` and the backend/frontend containers stay in sync with the working tree.

**Verification order**: Sync is not only a packaging step — **health checks and browser/manual QA against `http://localhost:3001` must assume the Compose stack has been updated** via `docker-dev-sync.sh` (or equivalent per `docs/workflow/DOCKER-LOCAL-AGENTS.md`). Do not record “verify pass” for Docker-based UI until sync has succeeded when sources changed.

Details and caveats (schema-only DB work, two-step equivalent): `docs/workflow/DOCKER-LOCAL-AGENTS.md` (item 11).
